elines dependency concerns return presentation, not the selected exception.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u22\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Risk-free and deposit-like advertising restrictions provide no gift exception.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u23\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Monitoring and possible future action supply neither an effective date nor an additional exception.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u24\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Institutional attribution.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u25\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Institutional attribution.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u26\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Institutional attribution.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u27\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Quoted offering-document requirement supports disclosure context; full Handbook is unavailable.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u28\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies the Code and its licensed-or-registered-person context.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u29\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies the missing FAQ and its issue date; its substantive answer cannot be inferred.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"DEFERRED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u30\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies changing supplementary advertising guidance, whose contents and applicable versions are unavailable.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"DEFERRED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u31\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"dimensions\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Both readings assess one benefit offered by an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, connected to promotion of a specific product or product type, including funds of particular fund houses. Public advertising and structured-product status are not prerequisites for this selected control.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u5\\\",\\\"u10\\\",\\\"u13\\\",\\\"u14\\\",\\\"u29\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"definitions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Gift classification and genuine fee-discount classification require judgment. Additional returns may be gifts but are not automatically gifts. Whether the discounted fees concern the promoted product is a separate fact, held stable across alternatives.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u8\\\",\\\"u13\\\",\\\"u14\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The parenthetical clearly excepts fee discounts from the gift restriction. Its unqualified wording supports discounts on any service, while the product-specific setting and anti-distraction purpose support a narrower, implied product-related limitation. The latter is less explicit. Section 103 authorisation or exemptions do not transfer to paragraph 3.11.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u10\\\",\\\"u13\\\",\\\"u14\\\",\\\"u15\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The selected control retains 'should not' as a regulatory restriction. A true result identifies an offer caught by that restriction, not a criminal offence or overall noncompliance. 'May be considered a gift' preserves classification uncertainty; the separate marketing 'must' and dealing-frequency best-endeavours language do not alter it.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u10\\\",\\\"u13\\\",\\\"u14\\\",\\\"u19\\\",\\\"u21\\\",\\\"u24\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"30 September 2010 dates the cited FAQ, not commencement of this circular or the gift restriction. No operative date or applicable version is supplied. The synthetic snapshot date supplies no legal commencement evidence; future guidance is expressly contemplated.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u24\\\",\\\"u30\\\",\\\"u31\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"dependencies\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"external-authorities.23ec46 is missing. The full paragraph 3.11 and FAQ answer are needed to resolve exception breadth and classification. The SFO, Handbook, paragraph 2.3 and Advertising Guidelines are separate dependencies, not grounds for expanding this selected control.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u10\\\",\\\"u12\\\",\\\"u14\\\",\\\"u15\\\",\\\"u21\\\",\\\"u22\\\",\\\"u28\\\",\\\"u29\\\",\\\"u30\\\",\\\"u31\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Does the applicable full paragraph 3.11 or the cited FAQ expressly limit discounts to fees or charges relating to the promoted product?\\\",\\n    \\\"What criteria distinguish a genuine fee reduction from an additional return or incentive described as a discount?\\\",\\n    \\\"Which circular, Code and FAQ versions apply at the assessment date?\\\",\\n    \\\"What are the comparator nodes’ actual expressions and fact definitions? DIFFERENT alone does not identify their interpretation, and INCOMPARABLE_FACT_BINDINGS does not establish a substantive legal disagreement.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"readings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\n        \\\"The assessment concerns one offered benefit in a distributor’s promotion of SFC-authorised funds.\\\",\\n        \\\"A genuine discount can be treated as excepted even where it otherwise falls within the assessed gift category.\\\",\\n        \\\"The unqualified words 'fees or charges' do not require those fees to relate to the promoted product.\\\",\\n        \\\"Unknown facts remain unknown; no missing classification is inferred from the diagnostic label.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\":[\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u1\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u14\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u13\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u15\\\"}\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"Retains the parent’s stronger literal reading: a genuine discount on unrelated service fees is excepted from this selected restriction. In the supplied snapshot, scope is true but the result remains unknown because is_fee_discount is unknown. The DIFFERENT label cannot justify assigning that fact. The hypothesis that a discount exception also clears section 103 fails because u13 and u15 preserve separate controls.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":{\\n        \\\"facts\\\":[\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds in the assessed activity.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"is_distributor\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u29\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed benefit is offered to a client in promotion of a specific fund or particular fund type, including a linkage to funds of certain fund houses.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"has_product_promotion_connection\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u14\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed benefit is offered and qualifies as a gift before applying the fee-discount exception; an additional return is not automatically classified as a gift.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"gift_offered\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u13\\\",\\\"u14\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed benefit genuinely constitutes a discount of fees or charges, irrespective of which service those fees concern.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"is_fee_discount\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u14\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The fees or charges discounted by the assessed benefit relate to the promoted investment product or product type.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"discount_relates_to_promoted_product\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u14\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"result\\\":\\\"(and gift_offered (not is_fee_discount))\\\",\\n        \\\"result_type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n        \\\"scope\\\":\\\"(and is_distributor has_product_promotion_connection)\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"local_id\\\":\\\"r1\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\":[\\n        \\\"Does the missing FAQ confirm or displace the literal absence of a product-related limitation on discounted fees?\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"statement\\\":\\\"Selected control: paragraph-10 gift-promotion restriction with an unqualified fee-discount exception. Within scope, an offered gift is caught unless it genuinely discounts fees or charges, including fees for another service. A true result concerns this restriction only.\\\",\\n      \\\"subject\\\":\\\"Unqualified fee-discount exception\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\n        \\\"The assessment concerns one offered benefit in a distributor’s promotion of SFC-authorised funds.\\\",\\n        \\\"A genuine discount can be treated as excepted even where it otherwise falls within the assessed gift category.\\\",\\n        \\\"The product-specific context and anti-distraction purpose imply that excepted fees or charges must relate to the promoted product or product type.\\\",\\n        \\\"This implied limitation is a provisional purposive reading, not an express condition in the retained wording.\\\",\\n        \\\"Unknown facts remain unknown; Boolean conclusions may nevertheless follow where a known fact makes an exception unavailable.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\":[\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u14\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"The purpose of the requirement is to avoid the use of gifts to distract investors from the features and risks of a particular product.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u14\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u14\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"3 The answer to question 1 of the frequently asked questions on the Code of Conduct issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u30\\\"}\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"Narrows the exception to reductions in costs relating to the promoted product. An unrelated-service discount can distract from that product’s risks like another promotional gift. In the supplied snapshot, scope and result are true because gift_offered is true and discount_relates_to_promoted_product is false, regardless of the unknown is_fee_discount. This distinguishes the rival from r1 without changing fact meanings. The strongest objection is that u14 never expressly says 'fees of the promoted product'; its purpose cannot conclusively supply those words.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":{\\n        \\\"facts\\\":[\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds in the assessed activity.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"is_distributor\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u29\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed benefit is offered to a client in promotion of a specific fund or particular fund type, including a linkage to funds of certain fund houses.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"has_product_promotion_connection\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u14\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed benefit is offered and qualifies as a gift before applying the fee-discount exception; an additional return is not automatically classified as a gift.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"gift_offered\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u13\\\",\\\"u14\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed benefit genuinely constitutes a discount of fees or charges, irrespective of which service those fees concern.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"is_fee_discount\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u14\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The fees or charges discounted by the assessed benefit relate to the promoted investment product or product type.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"discount_relates_to_promoted_product\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u14\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"result\\\":\\\"(and gift_offered (not (and is_fee_discount discount_relates_to_promoted_product)))\\\",\\n        \\\"result_type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n        \\\"scope\\\":\\\"(and is_distributor has_product_promotion_connection)\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"local_id\\\":\\\"r2\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\":[\\n        \\\"Does the missing authority support the implied product-related limitation despite the exception’s unqualified wording?\\\",\\n        \\\"If such a limitation exists, how does it apply to bundled account or platform fees covering several products?\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"statement\\\":\\\"Selected control: paragraph-10 gift-promotion restriction with a product-related fee-discount exception. Within scope, an offered gift is caught unless it genuinely discounts fees or charges relating to the promoted product or product type. A true result concerns this restriction only.\\\",\\n      \\\"subject\\\":\\\"Product-related fee-discount exception\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":35663,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":3191,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":0}}\n","fresh_context":true,"independence":"CONTEXT_ONLY_SAME_MODEL_CORRELATION_UNMEASURED","model":"gpt-6-astra","provider":"codex.fresh.v1","provider_route_hash":"3d676052ff208f9c0b35467659af41d3138476127d0d1b523970689c2edf4714","request_hash":"d58185f39b6e94b4f052b542dc3cda527a2826a617b24afb3579412e140251e9","response_hash":"418aba1b068e60953664bca1ab5d9964fc6aac251422594437413bdfaae800aa","transport_retry_policy":"NO_APPLICATION_RETRY; CLI transport behavior is external","usage":[{"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0,"input_tokens":35663,"output_tokens":3191,"reasoning_output_tokens":0}],"wall_milliseconds":111638},"response":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines distributors and the circular’s fund-promotion setting.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Examples of distributor-added features; does not define the discount exception.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Describes investment mandates without guaranteed rates; not an exception 